const postContent = "<h2>A Salary Slip Starts With Payroll Records</h2>\n<p>A payslip explains earnings and employee deductions for a specific period. Its appearance alone does not prove employment, payment or compliance. The responsible employer must review and authorize the record. A self-generated draft is not a substitute for the evidence requested by a bank, landlord or visa authority; confirm their requirements separately.</p>\n<p>The <a href=\"/tools/salary-slip\">Salary Slip Generator</a> now prepares a draft from entered payroll amounts. It does not automatically calculate tax, EOBI, provincial social security or provident fund. This scope was reviewed on21November2026. The earlier automatic tax calculation and fixed EOBI cap were removed rather than presented as current payroll rules.</p>\n<h2>Keep Earnings And Deductions Separate</h2>\n<p>Enter basic salary and each actual allowance separately. Their sum is gross earnings for this draft. The name of an allowance does not establish whether it is taxable or exempt. Do not assume a universal salary split or exemption percentage.</p>\n<p>Enter the employee income-tax withholding and employee EOBI deduction confirmed by payroll. Both fields require an explicit amount, including zero when applicable. Additional confirmed employee deductions can be totalled under a clear label. Employer-only contributions belong in the employer's records and must not automatically reduce employee pay.</p>\n<p>Eligibility, contribution bases, provincial rules, exemptions, adjustments and employer policies need separate verification. No EOBI, PESSI/SESSI or provident-fund rate is asserted by this guide. Ask the payroll professional which rules and period support each deduction.</p>\n<h2>A Synthetic Arithmetic Example</h2>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Entered item</th><th>PKR</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Basic salary</td><td>200,000</td></tr><tr><td>House rent allowance</td><td>30,000</td></tr><tr><td>Medical allowance</td><td>10,000</td></tr><tr><td>Conveyance</td><td>10,000</td></tr><tr><td>Gross earnings</td><td>250,000</td></tr><tr><td>Payroll-supplied income tax</td><td>23,000</td></tr><tr><td>Payroll-supplied employee EOBI</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>Other confirmed employee deductions</td><td>10,000</td></tr><tr><td>Total deductions</td><td>33,000</td></tr><tr><td>Draft net pay</td><td>217,000</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>These are invented inputs, not a tax or EOBI calculation. The draft reconciles250,000 minus33,000. Zero EOBI is an explicit example value, not an eligibility decision. If deductions exceed gross earnings, reconcile the records rather than issuing a negative-pay draft.</p>\n<h2>Estimate Tax Separately From Recorded Withholding</h2>\n<p>The <a href=\"/tools/tax-calculator\">year-specific salary tax calculator</a> provides a base planning estimate with stated limitations. Actual monthly withholding can differ because of payroll adjustments, variable earnings, prior deductions and applicable treatment. This generator does not infer taxable income from the total allowances or silently copy a planning estimate into a record.</p>\n<p>Primary reference checked21November2026: <a href=\"https://www.fbr.gov.pk/withholding-tax-rate-card/174298/174301\">FBR's current and previous withholding rate-card index</a> lists TY2027 as current and TY2026 as previous. Its <a href=\"https://download1.fbr.gov.pk/Docs/202681113864992WithholdingTaxRatesCard2027.pdf\">TY2027 rate card</a>, updated through30June2026 under Finance Act2026, was retrieved and its salary table reviewed on pages1–2. The card itself says the statute prevails. The previously referenced circular download timed out today; no new numeric tax rules were added to this generator or guide.</p>\n<h2>Review Before Printing</h2>\n<p>Check the pay period, employee and company details, allowance breakdown, deductions and net amount against the underlying payroll records. A printable footer keeps the draft status and calculation limits visible. Names and labels are text, not executable markup. Missing or invalid amounts prevent printing; explicitly enter zero where appropriate.</p>\n<p>Print opens a browser window. Save as PDF is an option in supported browser print dialogs, not a direct PDF or image export. Allow the window if it is blocked, then review the print preview. Actual mobile and print-dialog verification remains pending for this prepared version.</p>\n<h2>Protect Employee Information</h2>\n<p>The form uses page-memory state and loses inputs on reload. It has no saved employee profiles, database connector or email delivery. A downloaded or printed copy can still contain sensitive details: review its recipient and keep it private. Use synthetic information when testing the public tool.</p>\n<p>For a real payroll workflow, define authorized staff access, employee isolation, payroll-source integration, correction history and employer approval before adding storage or notifications. A clean draft is useful; it does not replace those controls.</p>"

